From: Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:04:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 56/59] arm64: dts: rockchip: h96-max-v58: stop watchdog before
 standby, IR wake

Power off ends in BL31 virtual-poweroff standby; the DesignWare watchdog
kept counting there and reset the board about 44 s later. With a CRU
reset on the node, dw_wdt_stop() asserts it, so systemd's disarm at
poweroff and the watchdog core's power-off notifier really stop it.
SRST_P_WDT0 resolves to 240 (SOFTRST_CON15 bit 0) in the vendor bit
index scheme registered by clk-rk3588.c.

List the remotectl interrupt lines (SPI 345 power-key match, SPI 344
channel) in rockchip,virtual-poweroff-irqs so BL31 keeps them as wake
sources in standby.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
index dd7418a7c..e18193f7f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
@@ -192,10 +192,17 @@ &uart9 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* CRU reset makes dw_wdt_stop() a real stop: systemd disarms at poweroff before standby */
 &wdt {
+	resets = <&cru SRST_P_WDT0>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* standby wake: remotectl power-key match (SPI 345) and channel (SPI 344) lines, as GIC INTIDs */
+&rockchip_suspend {
+	rockchip,virtual-poweroff-irqs = <377 376>;
+};
+
 /* HDMI0: CEC, external DDC bus, I2S path; HDMI1 not wired */
 &hdmi0 {
 	cec-enable;
